   "configuration_id": "as_scientific_ill_orange_cryostat_100mm",
   "key": "vacuum.available",
   "why": "Rejected because the ILL instruction manual contradicts 'cannot be evacuated'. Its sample-introduction procedure says to 'Connect a primary pump to the sample chamber valve' and 'pump it' before admitting 20 cc of helium exchange gas. The sample space can therefore be evacuated, but it operates in exchange gas. Under the vocabulary definition ('Sample space can be evacuated'), not_available/false is not supported. Re-express it as an exchange-gas requirement or mark it unknown."
  },
  {
   "configuration_id": "as_scientific_ill_orange_cryostat_100mm",
   "key": "pressure.base",
   "why": "Rejected because the claim of no evacuated sample space is contradicted: the manual has the sample chamber pumped with a primary pump. No base pressure is documented, so this should be unknown and not documented, not not_available."
  }
